  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "El La",
      "h2": "Two Genders",
      "body_html": "<p>Spanish uses <strong>el</strong> (m) and <strong>la</strong> (f). Most -o words are masculine ('el libro'), most -a are feminine ('la regla'). Learn the gender with each word.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Bag",
      "h2": "In My Bag",
      "body_html": "<p>'En mi mochila hay un libro y una regla' = 'In my bag there is a book and a ruler'. <strong>Un</strong> (m) and <strong>una</strong> (f) = a/an.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Many",
      "h2": "Plurals",
      "body_html": "<p>Add <strong>-s</strong> for plurals: <strong>los libros</strong> (the books), <strong>las reglas</strong> (the rulers). 'Los' (m) and 'las' (f) = the (plural).</p>"
    }
  ],
